thereof, without authority from the defendant as a corporation. If the judge erred in expressing his opinion as to the merits of the defence, that would not avail appellants, for it is the duty of this court \u201csimply to inquire whether there is any error in the judgment rendered, and not whether the reasons given to support it are sound.\u201d\nJudgment affirmed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice McIver,"}], "attorneys": ["Verdier Talbird, for appellants. Hlliott $ Howe, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "No. 1731.\nSmalls v. Benevolent Society of the Tabernacle Church of Beaufort.\nApril Term, 1885.\nJuly 20, 1885.\nVerdier Talbird, for appellants. Hlliott $ Howe, contra."}, "file_name": "0602-01", "first_page_order": 610, "last_page_order": 611}